(dp8
VThis information can be collected during various interactions such as when user creates or modifies their account, request on-demand services, contact customer support, or otherwise communicate with us directly or indirectly.
p9
I1
sVWhen user request Zum services, our Zumers may provide us with a User rating after providing services to user.
p10
I1
sVFor example, Zum share user\u2019s name, photo (if user provide one), average User rating given by Zumers, and pickup and/or drop-off locations with Zumers;
p11
I1
sVWith third parties with whom user choose to let us share information, for example other apps or websites that integrate with our API or Services, or those with an API or Service with which Zum integrate; and
p12
I1
sVCalifornia law permits residents of California to request certain details about how their information is shared with third parties for direct marketing purposes.
p13
I1
sVAs a user, if you (parent or person authorized by parent)register a child as a family member (collectively termed as \u201cuser\u201d henceforth), we\u2019ll request that you provide us with certain information (including PII) that can be used to identify such person, such as name, photo, age, phone number, and email address.
p14
I1
sVZumers will have access to a Zum-provided phone number to allow the Zumers to communicate with such users, including users who are children (however, the user\u2019s actual phone number will not be provided directly to the Zumer), the user\u2019s first name and last name, photo, schedule.
p15
I1
sVIf user opt out, Zum may still send user non-promotional communications, such as those about user\u2019s account, about Services user have requested, or our ongoing business relations.
